<http://digistrucmed.org/normative-assertion/lu_1d4ae21bdadbacafa8087e019976dde180c346c5d4626772c2b286528336efac_n0010/na_0062> <http://digistrucmed.org/applicabilityExceptionStatus> "NONE_STATED" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/grade-record/lu_1d4ae21bdadbacafa8087e019976dde180c346c5d4626772c2b286528336efac_n0010/gr_0060> <http://digistrucmed.org/hasGradeValue> <http://digistrucmed.org/ClassOfRecommendation_III> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_1d4ae21bdadbacafa8087e019976dde180c346c5d4626772c2b286528336efac_n0010/tu_0004> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "A stepwise treatment-intensification approach aiming at intensive risk factor treatment is recommended for apparently healthy people at high or very high ASCVD risk, as well as patients with established ASCVD and/or DM, with consideration of CVD risk, treatment benefit of risk factors, risk modifiers, comorbidities, and patient preferences." .
<http://digistrucmed.org/MedicationEntity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_1d4ae21bdadbacafa8087e019976dde180c346c5d4626772c2b286528336efac_n0010/tu_0027> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "In treated patients aged ≥70 years, it is recommended that SBP should generally be targeted to <140 and down to 130 mmHg if tolerated." .
<http://digistrucmed.org/normative-assertion/lu_1d4ae21bdadbacafa8087e019976dde180c346c5d4626772c2b286528336efac_n0010/na_0029> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://digistrucmed.org/NormativeAssertion> .
